**3. How last-one-wins is resolved:**
A single `int prefix_mode` variable is updated each time `-H` (sets to 1) or `-h` (sets to -1) is encountered during argument parsing. After all arguments are processed, the final value of `prefix_mode` determines the prefix decision: `1` → always prefix, `-1` → never prefix, `0` → default rule (prefix if ≥2 files). This guarantees consistency because there is only one value to consult.

